  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "The star – pass two lines over",
  "description": "Five lines stand in a large pentagon in the half court: one at half-court, two out on the wings and two down by the baseline on either side of the lane. The ball never goes to the next line but to the line two along, so the passes draw a star. After the pass the passer runs to the back of the line they passed to.\n\nStart with one ball and add a second once it flows. Change direction after a while.\n\nWith a finish: when the ball reaches the line at half-court, the receiver dribbles straight in for a lay-up, takes the rebound and passes out to the next line so the star keeps going. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look at the receiver before you pass – the ball should arrive at chest height."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Meet the ball with hands ready and turn towards the next line as you catch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Run straight after the pass and stay out of the ball's path."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The lay-up: full speed to the basket and finish with the correct hand."
    }
  ],
